{"id":"sh/0ju10nux","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":26,"width":1140,"height":26},"text":"PERIGEE   /   OUR CONTRIBUTION","style":{"fontSize":17,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/rel03ytg","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":65,"width":1184,"height":66},"text":"A saved explanation with the data behind it","style":{"fontSize":42,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/qdcjudcv","kind":"shape","position":{"left":48,"top":678,"width":1184,"height":1},"geometry":"rect","fillColor":"#343B3B","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/dg3i58bm","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":691,"width":1010,"height":19},"text":"NASA Space Apps 2026. Planet X and SPHEREx.","style":{"fontSize":14,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#AFB6BA","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/sfu1w3u1","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":1168,"top":689,"width":70,"height":23},"text":"6 / 7","style":{"fontSize":16,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#AFB6BA","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/3q10zytk","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":159,"width":553,"height":37},"text":"One continuous investigation","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/ipszqtcz","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":204,"width":553,"height":155},"text":"Perigee connects image comparison, scientific checks and learner-written reasoning in one workflow. The learner chooses an interpretation and explains it using the selected observations. The reference appears after they record their own thinking.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/ml8j2twr","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":404,"width":553,"height":37},"text":"Someone else can inspect the reasoning","style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/7m1kbyxc","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":449,"width":553,"height":187},"text":"Each export retains the observation IDs, dates, wavelengths, quality results, archive URLs, raw-file SHA-256 fingerprints and processing details. The notes autosave in the browser. JSON preserves the structured record; printing creates a PDF for a teacher, classmate or club.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/8na143ex","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":164,"width":561,"height":28},"text":"EXAMPLE COMPLETED EVIDENCE CARD","style":{"fontSize":18,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#D7FC70","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/9oj2d8f2","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":215,"width":561,"height":32},"text":"Observation","style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/upsj6twn","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":254,"width":561,"height":70},"text":"In images A and C, the bright glow shifts north relative to the surrounding stars.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#AFB6BA","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/vq1kfyx8","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":350,"width":561,"height":32},"text":"Explanation","style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/wra183et","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":390,"width":561,"height":70},"text":"The shift is consistent with Barnard’s Star moving across the sky, as the catalog predicts.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#AFB6BA","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/hcj2h8ve","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":485,"width":561,"height":32},"text":"Evidence and uncertainty","style":{"fontSize":24,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#F5F6F5","bold":true,"alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/idsjadwz","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":671,"top":526,"width":561,"height":112},"text":"A: 25 Aug 2025, 2.0062 µm. C: 19 Aug 2026, 2.0284 µm. The core is saturated, so its exact center is uncertain. The exported card links both observations to IRSA.","style":{"fontSize":23,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#AFB6BA","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0},
{"id":"sh/3elkjidk","kind":"textbox","position":{"left":48,"top":649,"width":1184,"height":24},"text":"Illustrative completed record, not a user testimonial. The contribution is the integrated reasoning workflow and retained provenance.","style":{"fontSize":14,"typeface":"Avenir Next","color":"#AFB6BA","alignment":"left"},"geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0}
]}
